\f0\fs24 \cf0 When the device is powered on, it starts in synthesizer mode.\
\
To begin, press the REC button to enter step sequencer mode.\
To set a "Trig Condition," press EDIT while in step sequencer mode; the 4th knob will then control the "trig cond" parameter.\
Select a step; to change its note, hold the step down and turn the 1st knob.\
To adjust velocity, hold the step and turn the 2nd knob. The 3rd knob controls the trigger duration (gate length), and the 4th knob sets the probability.\
\
OP1 \'96 Trigger and note editor\
OP2 \'96 Oscillator editor\
OP3 \'96 Amplifier editor\
OP4 \'96 Filter editor\
\
FX \'96 Effects settings (holding the button displays effect pages across the sequencer steps)\
SEL \'96 Channel selection, voice limit settings, and channel volume\
ENV \'96 Envelopes for oscillator 1 and 2 amplifiers, plus one assignable ADSR envelope (press HOME to access the destination/DEST setting)\
LFO \'96 8 LFOs, assignable to any parameter; hold HOME while in LFO mode to access additional settings\
EDIT \'96 Switches between pattern banks\
HOME \'96 Functions similarly to a SHIFT or FUNC key\
SAVE \'96 Saves the pattern\
SEQ \'96 Sequencer settings; allows you to configure length, pages, step boundaries, and playback modes (forward, backward, pendulum, or random)\
PLAY/STOP \'96 Starts or stops playback. Pressing HOME + PLAY allows you to edit the pattern tempo, toggle the metronome, adjust its volume, and set a metronome pre-roll (count-in)\
\
Holding OP1 reveals two pages: the first is the current view, while the second allows you to configure filter and LFO triggers, as well as portamento settings (including activation and time). Holding OP2: 4 pages. The first is your current location; the second page allows you to adjust the sub-oscillator detune, as well as the oscillator's pitch and volume. The third and fourth pages provide the same controls for the second oscillator.\
Holding OP3: The first is your current location; the second page is for managing effect sends; the third page is the transient shaper (available independently for each channel).\
Holding OP4: The first is your current location (filter for the first oscillator); the second page is the filter for the second oscillator; the third page is the envelope for the first filter; the fourth page is the envelope for the second filter.\
Holding FX: The first page is for delay settings, the second for reverb, and the third for chorus.\
\
In the SEQ menu (sequencer settings), pressing HOME opens the Euclidean Sequencer and its configuration options.\
A single press of EDIT switches the pattern.\
Holding EDIT switches the pattern bank.}